{"id":"act-4","label":"Act 4","blocks":[{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 1"},{"k":"d","text":"An obscure cavern, which through winding paths leads out of the infernal regions."},{"k":"d","text":"ORPHEUS and EURYDICE."},{"k":"d","text":"ORPHEUS, holding EURYDICE by the hand, but without raising his eyes to her face, appears in the distance, and advances tremblingly."},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ah, come, Eurydice,","It is I. You, the most sweet","And constant object of my love, ah! come."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Is it you? truly you?","It is not a dream of mine?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["No, you really see your love.","It is I, still alive,","And descended into this place","To take you from the dead.","Jupiter felt pity","For my great sorrow,","You shall return to life."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Shall I live again?","O gods! what goodness!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Eurydice, let us go,","Let us hasten to enjoy","This boon of heaven.","Let us depart from this","Abode of death.","You are no more a shade,","And the torch of love","Still burns within my heart."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["What do I hear? Can this be true?","O happy fate!","We shall again be united","In the sweet bonds of love!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ah! yes. But let us go,","Let us no more delay."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["But, heaven! No more I feel your hand.","Am I no more the one","You one day loved so dearly?","The former love for Eurydice","Has left your heart?","Or you find no more in me","My former beauty?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"d","text":"aside"},{"k":"v","lines":["Alas! what forbiddance!","Eurydice, let us go,","Let us now leave this place.","(I would show her","The extent of my affection.","But, cruel law!","Barbarous fate!)"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["A single look I implore.","Are these the happy days","You have prepared for me?","Is this the sweet reward","Of my faithful love?","Oh, cruel thought! Orpheus! Alas!","You now refuse","The tender sighs","Of your beloved!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Torment me no more with your doubts."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["You bring me back to life","To bring me again to grief.","Take back your gift,","Cruel one, leave me!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Come, come to your consort."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["No, never! Death I prefer","To living again with you."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["See my sorrow!"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Leave me in peace!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["No, my life, forever","I shall follow you."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Why, then, are you so cruel?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["I must die first","Than say my reason."]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE and ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Oh, gods, help me!","Behold my tears!","Alas! no more","I can my grief endure."]},{"k":"d","text":"ORPHEUS, plunged in the greatest grief, leans against a rock."},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"d","text":"aside"},{"k":"v","lines":["But why does he persist","In keeping silent?","What secret does he hide?","From the abode of peace","Shall he take me only","To insult me with indifference?"]},{"k":"v","lines":["O barbarous fate!","To make me a prey","Of bitterer tears","You take me away."]},{"k":"v","lines":["I was enjoying","A tranquil peace,","But grief again","Has now my bosom seized."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Her vain suspicion","Augments my sorrow.","What shall I say? What shall I do?","I am almost in despair.","How can I now calm","The anxiety of my mind?"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["I vacillate, I tremble,","I lose my strength, I sigh!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Who does not pity me?","My courage fails!"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Oh, barbarous fate! etc."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Oh, most cruel trial!"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["You leave me, Orpheus,","No pity you feel for me."]},{"k":"v","lines":["Your desolate wife","In vain calls for aid.","Hear ye, o gods, my just complaints,","Must I again from life depart,","And not obtain from him a single look?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["I can no more resist,","I lose my reason.","Transported by my love,","I forget the forbiddance,","Eurydice, and myself."]},{"k":"d","text":"ORPHEUS makes a movement as to look back, then withdraws."},{"k":"v","lines":["What do I?"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["My love, I scarcely","Can find now breath."]},{"k":"d","text":"She falls against a rock."},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Despair not.","You must, then, know? But what do I?","Merciful Gods! My grief will never end?"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Be this my last adieu!","Do not forget Eurydice."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ah! where am I? Where is my courage now?","Who ever endured such woes?","O my beloved Eurydice!"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Orpheus! alas! I die!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Oh, unhappy me!","In what dreadful state","This love has thrown my heart."]},{"k":"v","lines":["Dear love! Eurydice!","Alas! she dies, oh fatal day!","I shall see her no more!","And I have caused her death.","Oh cruel law! Oh impious fate!","This is above all grief.","In such a fatal hour","Despair and death","Is all that’s left to me."]},{"k":"v","lines":["What shall I do without Eurydice?","Where shall I go without my love?","Eurydice! O Gods! answer me,","I am still your faithful lover."]},{"k":"v","lines":["Eurydice, alas! all hopes are gone!","No aid I can expect,","Neither on this earth nor from heaven!","Oh fatal silence!","Now all is lost,","Now forever","My heart is broken!"]},{"k":"v","lines":["Forever now she is departed!","A ray of hope does not remain.","To mourn and cry is now my share,","To call for aid it would be vain."]},{"k":"v","lines":["But I can still my woes suspend,","Yes, with my life my grief can end.","This cruel fate","I could never bear!"]},{"k":"v","lines":["I still am near the gates of death,","I soon will have","Rejoined my love.","Ah! yes, I come","To thee, forever I come.","No more from me thou shalt be stolen;","My death again","Will take me to thy side."]},{"k":"d","text":"ORPHEUS draws the sword to kill himself, but LOVE, who suddenly appears to him, prevents the blow."},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 2"},{"k":"d","text":"LOVE, ORPHEUS and EURYDICE."},{"k":"s","text":"LOVE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Suspend, Orpheus."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Heaven!","What power have you","To stop me in my deed?"]},{"k":"s","text":"LOVE"},{"k":"v","lines":["You must your fury calm!","Recognize in my presence Love,","Who watches over your fate."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["What do you want from me?"]},{"k":"s","text":"LOVE"},{"k":"v","lines":["I found in you","True constancy and faith,","Your sufferings must end."]},{"k":"d","text":"LOVE touches EURYDICE, and reanimates her."},{"k":"v","lines":["Eurydice, return to life!","Of the most constant heart,","Gain the due reward."]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"d","text":"with transport"},{"k":"v","lines":["Oh, Eurydice!"]},{"k":"s","text":"EURYDICE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Orpheus!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORPHEUS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Merciful Gods!","How can I praise your goodness!"]},{"k":"s","text":"LOVE"},{"k":"v","lines":["No more deny","The power of Love.","From the abode of darkness","I come to save you.","From now you can enjoy","What favors love can give."]},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 3"},{"k":"d","text":"Enter the suite of ORPHEUS and EURYDICE."},{"k":"d","text":"Hymn to LOVE."},{"k":"s","text":"ALL"},{"k":"v","lines":["It is the God of Paphus","That animates the world,","’Tis he who in the air","Overtakes the rapid bird;","He does inflame the Nereids,","Even in the ocean’s depth;","He cheers the youth,","And grace he adds to beauty;","He gives more charm to wisdom,","And spreads his path with flowers;","It is he who consoles us.","When even we lose his favors,","Since when he flies from us","He always leaves us friendship","All losses to repair."]}]}